{{Politics of Okaiken}}

The {{Nihongo|'''Ikazaki Cabinet'''|五十崎内閣|Ikazaki Naikaku}}, officially the 110th Cabinet of Okaiken, is the current executive government of Okaiken. Formed on 20 May 2026 following the [[Okaiken general election, 2026|2026 general election]], it is a three-party coalition between the [[Sanese Communist Party|Sanese Communist Party (SCP)]], the [[Okaiken Socialist Party]] (OSP), and the [[Social Democratic Party (Okaiken)|Social Democratic Party (SDP)]], with the confidence and supply support of independent member [[Hayashi Akihiro]] (Ogasawara-3rd). The coalition holds 251 seats in the [[House of Commoners of Okaiken|House of Commoners]], a supermajority of 13 seats over the 238 required for governance.

The cabinet is led by Prime Minister [[Kousuke Ikazaki]] (SCP) and Deputy Prime Minister [[Rento Nakayama]] (OSP), who previously served as Health Minister in the collapsed [[Honda-Nakayama Cabinet]]. It is the first cabinet in Sanese history to operate under a formal gender composition threshold—the {{Nihongo|'''Yoshida Threshold'''|吉田閾値|Yoshida Shiki-ichi}}—requiring at least 40% of ministerial positions to be held by women.

==Formation==
{{main|Okaiken general election, 2026}}
The 2026 general election, triggered by the collapse of the Honda-Nakayama Cabinet following the [[Nakayama Station dragging incident|March Maelstrom]], produced a decisive rejection of the [[Progressive Party of Okaiken|Progressive Party (PPO)]] and the [[Liberal Democratic Party (Okaiken)|LDP]]. The SCP won 115 seats, the OSP won 100, and the SDP won 36, giving the three parties a combined 251 seats—13 more than the 238 required for an absolute majority.

The coalition was negotiated over three days of intense talks, dubbed the {{Nihongo|"Three-Day War"|三日間の戦争|Mikkakan no Sensō}} by political commentators. The central tension was between the SCP's demand for a "fortress" cabinet focused on institutional accountability and the OSP's insistence on a "social mandate" that prioritised welfare expansion and the Two-Man Mandate. The SDP, led by [[Shimane Yoshida]], entered negotiations on the second day and extracted two binding conditions: the Yoshida Threshold (40% women in cabinet) and the creation of a dedicated Minister for Gender Equality and Democratic Accountability.

The final agreement was reached at 06:47 on 19 May 2026, following a 47-minute telephone call between Nakayama and Ikazaki that began at 06:00. The cabinet was formally sworn in on 20 May 2026.

